<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia to offer A$900 mln in T-bonds.</title>
<headline>Australia to offer A$900 mln in T-bonds.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Treasury will offer a total of A$900 million in Treasury bonds through a tender on Tuesday, the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) said.  </p>
<p>The offering will comprise A$300 million of 8.75 percent bonds maturing in January 2001 and A$600 million of 6.75 percent bonds maturing in November 2006.</p>
<p>The bank said bids would be received until 12.45 p.m. (0145 GMT) on Tuesday and results will be announced at 2.00 p.m. (0300 GMT). Settlement date is February 13.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
